#if($page.id.toString() == "381890661")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">What has changed</span><p>Use the resource pages for current files and availability. Older announcements are not evidence that a release is ready.</p></div></div><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Looking for the latest resource?</h2><p>Open its source page and check the file and review information.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Templates & Assets')" class="text-link">Browse resources</a></aside><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Older announcements</summary><div><p>The existing announcements need review before they can be used as a current release log. <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Archive')" class="">Open archive guidance</a>.</p></div></details>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381890664")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Historical reference</span><p>No verified release history is presented in this review build.</p></div></div><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Need a previous version?</h2><p>Include the resource name and the version or date you need.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="text-link">Ask for an earlier release ↗</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891652")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">How we work</span><p>Start with an existing resource. If you need new work or a review, bring a clear brief.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Submitting a Request')" class="button">Prepare a request</a></div><div class="choice-grid"><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Templates & Assets')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h2>Use existing material</h2><p>Templates, slides, logos and media.</p><span class="choice-go">Find a resource <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'What We Can Help With')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h2>Scope creative work</h2><p>Understand what to bring and what needs agreement.</p><span class="choice-go">Check the scope <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Turnaround Times')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h2>Plan the timing</h2><p>Agree the use date, inputs and review stages.</p><span class="choice-go">Plan the work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a></div>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891657")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Help and next steps</span><p>Short answers to the most common Hub questions.</p></div></div><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Where are templates and slides?</summary><div><p>Start with <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Templates & Assets')" class="">Templates and assets</a>. The source pages show file availability. Presentation releases belong in the Hub.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Where are photos and video?</summary><div><p>Use <a href="https://skao.canto.global/v/SKAOLibrary?from_main_library" class="">the Canto library ↗</a> and check each asset’s credit and permitted use.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Can I adapt material myself?</summary><div><p>Follow the release’s usage notes and keep credits. Ask the relevant content owner about changes to facts or meaning; ask Creative Production about substantial design work.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Who approves the work?</summary><div><p>Identify the appropriate content owner and final reviewer in the brief. The approval route depends on the work and should be confirmed rather than assumed.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Can I get an urgent turnaround?</summary><div><p>Explain the use date and any flexibility. <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Turnaround Times')" class="">Scope and timing need agreement</a>.</p></div></details><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Still stuck?</h2><p>Include the relevant page or asset link.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="text-link">Ask for help ↗</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891673")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Do it with confidence</span><p>Practical checks for work you can prepare using existing resources.</p></div></div><div class="choice-grid"><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Formatting a Presentation')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h2>Prepare slides</h2><p>Structure, sources and accessibility.</p><span class="choice-go">Read the slide guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Making Your Own Poster')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h2>Make a poster</h2><p>Choose a layout and check the output.</p><span class="choice-go">Read the poster guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h2>Prepare print files</h2><p>Get the supplier specifications right.</p><span class="choice-go">Read the print guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a></div>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891678")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Self-service guide</span><p>Start with a suitable template and build the talk around your audience.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Slide Decks & Presentations')" class="button">Find presentation resources</a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Build the story</h2><ul><li>Give each slide a clear purpose and use readable, concise headings.</li><li>Use the supplied layouts and keep spacing, alignment and typography consistent.</li><li>Use imagery and charts to explain the message; retain their sources and credits.</li></ul></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Check before presenting</h2><ul><li>Try the deck on the intended display and check that text and charts are readable from the audience’s position.</li><li>Check contrast, alternative text and reading order. Caption any video.</li><li>Check facts, dates and any adapted claims with the appropriate content owner.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Need more than formatting?</h2><p>Bring the draft and audience brief.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Submitting a Request')" class="text-link">Ask for a review</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891681")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Self-service guide</span><p>Confirm the organiser’s dimensions and output requirements before choosing a layout.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Poster Templates')" class="button">Check poster templates</a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Prepare the content</h2><ul><li>Decide the main message, title, authors and the information the audience needs.</li><li>Use readable headings, a clear reading order and enough space around figures.</li><li>Keep credits and sources with images and charts.</li></ul></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Prepare the output</h2><ul><li>Confirm print size, orientation and submission format with the organiser or supplier.</li><li>Check image resolution at the intended size and proof the exported file.</li><li>Confirm colour, bleed and delivery requirements with the supplier.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Sending it to print?</h2><p>Use the actual supplier requirements.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')" class="text-link">Check print preparation</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891685")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Before supplier handoff</span><p>Use the supplier’s specifications for the actual product. A single export recipe does not fit every print job.</p></div></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Confirm the specification</h2><ol><li>Finished dimensions, trim, bleed and safe area.</li><li>Colour profile and any spot colours or special finishes.</li><li>Required PDF standard, image resolution and font handling.</li><li>Proof process, quantity, final artwork deadline and delivery details.</li></ol></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Check the exported file</h2><ul><li>Review text, page order, dimensions and image quality.</li><li>Check fonts, colour and overprint settings as appropriate to the supplier’s workflow.</li><li>Get the required content and artwork approvals before production.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Need production support?</h2><p>Send the specification and draft artwork, with any unresolved questions.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Submitting a Request')" class="text-link">Brief the print work</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891661")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">New work or a review</span><p>Already have a brief? Send it through the creative helpdesk with your files or source links.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="button">Open creative helpdesk ↗</a></div><div class="process-strip"><span><b>1</b> Describe the need</span><span><b>2</b> Submit in Jira</span><span><b>3</b> Agree scope and timing</span></div><details class="brief-builder"><summary>Need help writing the brief?</summary><div class="builder-content"><p>Use this optional helper, then copy the result into Jira. It does not submit a request.</p><p class="form-note">Fields marked * are required. Your draft is not saved and is lost if you leave or reload.</p><form id="briefForm" hidden><div class="form-grid"><label class="field">Project *<input name="Project" required maxlength="3000" type="text"><small>What is the work called?</small></label><label class="field">Use date *<input name="Use date" required maxlength="3000" type="text"><small>When will it be used, and why then?</small></label><label class="field">Purpose and audience *<textarea name="Purpose and audience" required maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>What should this help people understand or do?</small></label><label class="field">Outputs and scope *<textarea name="Outputs and scope" required maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>What do you need? Include format, quantity and what is out of scope.</small></label><label class="field">Content and review owners<textarea name="Content and review owners"  maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>Who supplies the content and who approves the result?</small></label><label class="field">Inputs and constraints<textarea name="Inputs and constraints"  maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>Source links, budget, rights, missing information and dependencies.</small></label></div><button class="button" type="submit">Prepare my request</button></form><section id="draftPanel" hidden><h2 id="draftHeading" tabindex="-1">Your request draft</h2><p>Review the wording, copy it, then submit it in the helpdesk. A request is not booked until scope and timing are confirmed.</p><pre class="output" id="briefOutput"></pre><div class="actions"><button id="copyBrief" class="button" type="button">Copy request text</button><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="button secondary">Open helpdesk to submit</a></div><p id="copyStatus" class="status" role="status"></p></section></div></details><noscript><p>Use the creative helpdesk directly. The optional brief helper needs JavaScript.</p></noscript><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>What makes a useful brief?</summary><div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Include these essentials</h2><ul><li>Purpose, audience and the real use date.</li><li>Outputs, formats and what is outside the scope.</li><li>Draft content, source material and any missing inputs.</li><li>Content owner, final reviewer, budget and supplier constraints.</li></ul></section></div></details><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>A request is the start of a conversation</h2><p>The team confirms capacity, scope and delivery timing after review.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Turnaround Times')" class="text-link">How timing is agreed</a></aside><p class="quiet-note">Planning an event? <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Events Support')" class="">Brief the creative materials</a>. Event logistics stay with the events team.</p>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891666")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Planning the work</span><p>Give the actual use date and explain what depends on it. Delivery timing is agreed after the brief and capacity are reviewed.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Submitting a Request')" class="button">Send the brief</a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>What affects the schedule</h2><ul><li>When usable content and source files will be ready.</li><li>The output, complexity and amount of adaptation required.</li><li>Who reviews the work and when they can respond.</li><li>Supplier production, delivery and other dependencies.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>An urgent request?</h2><p>State the real deadline, its reason and what can be reduced. Urgency does not automatically create a delivery commitment.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="text-link">Open the helpdesk ↗</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891669")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Scope and responsibilities</span><p>Creative Production helps shape and produce agreed creative materials. The brief determines the work and the capacity required.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Submitting a Request')" class="button">Discuss the creative work</a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Examples to discuss</h2><ul><li>Design and layout for publications, presentations and graphics.</li><li>Video, animation and creative digital work.</li><li>Visual identity, templates and reusable resources.</li><li>Creative materials for events, print and displays.</li></ul></section><div class="responsibility-split"><section><h2>Bring the content</h2><p>The requester supplies the purpose, audience, draft or source material and the appropriate content reviewer.</p></section><section><h2>Agree the production</h2><p>The team confirms the outputs, responsibilities, timing and any supplier requirements.</p></section></div><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Event logistics or editorial ownership?</h2><p>Use the responsible team’s route. A creative brief does not transfer all project responsibilities to Creative Production.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Events Support')" class="text-link">See event responsibilities</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891606")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">A consistent SKAO identity</span><p>Start from the official artwork and the Brand Book. Use these essentials as a quick reference.</p></div></div><div class="brand-specimens"><div class="colour-spec navy"><strong>Blueshift Navy</strong><div class="copy-row"><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="#070068" aria-label="Copy Blueshift Navy hex #070068"><code>#070068</code><span>Copy</span></button><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="7, 0, 104" aria-label="Copy Blueshift Navy RGB 7, 0, 104"><code>RGB 7, 0, 104</code><span>Copy</span></button></div></div><div class="colour-spec magenta"><strong>Redshift Magenta</strong><div class="copy-row"><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="#E70068" aria-label="Copy Redshift Magenta hex #E70068"><code>#E70068</code><span>Copy</span></button><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="231, 0, 104" aria-label="Copy Redshift Magenta RGB 231, 0, 104"><code>RGB 231, 0, 104</code><span>Copy</span></button></div></div><div class="type-spec"><span class="type-sample" aria-hidden="true">Aa</span><strong>Noto Sans</strong><small>Fallback: Verdana</small></div></div><div class="choice-grid"><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Logos & Icons')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h2>Logo artwork</h2><p>Find the supplied files and choose a suitable version.</p><span class="choice-go">Find logo files <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Colour Palette and Typography')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h2>Colours and type</h2><p>Digital colour values and practical typography guidance.</p><span class="choice-go">Check the essentials <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'SKAO Brand Book')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h2>Brand Book</h2><p>The source for detailed rules and applications.</p><span class="choice-go">Open the source page <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a></div><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Working with partner brands</summary><div><p>Use the current guidance for the specific partner and application. Do not assemble a new logo lock-up from memory.</p><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Co-Branding CSIRO')" class="">CSIRO co-branding</a> · <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Co-Branding SARAO')" class="">SARAO co-branding</a></div></details><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Need a second pair of eyes?</h2><p>Include the draft, intended use and partner requirements.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="text-link">Ask about the brand ↗</a></aside>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891610")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Practical application</span><p>Use the existing templates and artwork to keep your work recognisably SKAO.</p></div></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>A quick self-check</h2><ul><li>Logo: supplied artwork, correct variant, clear space and original proportions.</li><li>Type: Noto Sans, with Verdana as fallback.</li><li>Colour: the sourced palette and readable contrast.</li><li>Images: relevant to the message, with asset-specific credits and permissions.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Start from existing material</h2><p>Choose a template rather than rebuilding the layout.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Templates & Assets')" class="text-link">Find a resource</a></aside>
