<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Brand essentials</span><p>Use these digital values from the retained SKAO Brand Book v2, March 2022.</p></div></div><div class="brand-specimens"><div class="colour-spec navy"><strong>Blueshift Navy</strong><div class="copy-row"><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="#070068" aria-label="Copy Blueshift Navy hex #070068"><code>#070068</code><span>Copy</span></button><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="7, 0, 104" aria-label="Copy Blueshift Navy RGB 7, 0, 104"><code>RGB 7, 0, 104</code><span>Copy</span></button></div></div><div class="colour-spec magenta"><strong>Redshift Magenta</strong><div class="copy-row"><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="#E70068" aria-label="Copy Redshift Magenta hex #E70068"><code>#E70068</code><span>Copy</span></button><button type="button" class="copy-value" data-copy="231, 0, 104" aria-label="Copy Redshift Magenta RGB 231, 0, 104"><code>RGB 231, 0, 104</code><span>Copy</span></button></div></div><div class="type-spec"><span class="type-sample" aria-hidden="true">Aa</span><strong>Noto Sans</strong><small>Fallback: Verdana</small></div></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Apply colour carefully</h2><ul><li>Use navy for text and links on light backgrounds. Magenta works well as an accent; check each text/background pairing.</li><li>For print, use the Brand Book and the supplier’s agreed colour specifications rather than guessing CMYK or Pantone conversions.</li><li>Use labels, symbols or patterns as well as colour to communicate meaning.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Need Noto Sans?</h2><p>Use the official font source or your organisation’s approved installation route.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Font Downloads')" class="text-link">Find font guidance</a></aside>
