<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Creative support for events</span><p>Start with the audience, purpose and use date. Reuse existing material before commissioning something new.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Submitting a Request')" class="button">Brief the creative work</a></div><div class="responsibility-split"><section><h2>Creative materials</h2><p>Presentation design, stand graphics, print, signage or video within an agreed brief.</p></section><section><h2>Event organisation</h2><p>Registration, attendance, travel, staffing and logistics remain with the events team.</p></section></div><div class="choice-grid"><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Event Planning Checklist')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h2>Prepare the package</h2><p>Gather specifications, content and review dates.</p><span class="choice-go">Use the checklist <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Stand Design and Materials')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h2>Stand graphics</h2><p>Brief an existing kit or a new visual layout.</p><span class="choice-go">Plan the stand <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a><a class="choice-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Print Materials')"><span class="choice-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h2>Print or merchandise</h2><p>Confirm purpose, quantity and supplier requirements.</p><span class="choice-go">Plan print materials <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a></div><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Before committing to production</summary><div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Confirm with the responsible teams</h2><ul><li>Venue and supplier specifications, dimensions and delivery requirements.</li><li>Content owner, proof reviewer and budget approval.</li><li>Supplier lead time and the final artwork deadline.</li><li>Applicable safety requirements with the event organiser and HSSE.</li></ul></section><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Health and Safety')" class="">Find the HSSE route</a> · <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Merchandise and Giveaways')" class="">Merchandise guidance</a></div></details>
